product and I'm going to leave.

00:35:53.766 --> 00:35:56.966
This one is nominal, but I'm
now I'm going to change these levels,

00:35:57.933 --> 00:35:59.833
so I'm actually going
to change these labels.

00:35:59.833 --> 00:36:06.200
So for instance, I click right here, add
one, and that's usually strongly disagree.

00:36:06.200 --> 00:36:09.100
And then the two is disagree.

00:36:10.966 --> 00:36:14.933
The three might be neither,

00:36:14.933 --> 00:36:18.433
four would be agree

00:36:18.433 --> 00:36:21.433
and five might be

00:36:21.433 --> 00:36:23.766
strongly agree.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:25.766
A lot of people call this a Likert scale.

00:36:25.766 --> 00:36:27.333
It's actually a response scale.

00:36:27.333 --> 00:36:30.500
Likert scales have more to do
with how you choose the questions

00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:34.066
as opposed to the format
in which you respond to them.

00:36:34.066 --> 00:36:36.066
But call it a Likert scale if you want.

00:36:36.066 --> 00:36:38.000
It's a 1 to 5 rating scale,

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:42.100
and then you can see that
these labels all show up down here.

00:36:42.100 --> 00:36:44.766
That's really the convenient thing.

00:36:44.766 --> 00:36:47.666
And remember,
the numbers are still underneath there,

00:36:47.666 --> 00:36:50.666
so you can still do numerical operations
on these variables.

00:36:51.033 --> 00:36:54.166
The last one I want to show you
is this text variable.

00:36:54.166 --> 00:36:58.400
At the end you see says nominal text
because I actually typed in the letters

00:36:58.800 --> 00:37:02.233
Y and N
