00:37:02.233 --> 00:37:04.933
I can click on the Y, I can put subscribed

00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:09.400
and I can maybe put they're

00:37:09.400 --> 00:37:11.933
not subscribe or they can't be websites
I will call my visitor.

00:37:12.833 --> 00:37:18.533
And so now you have new names
for the variables.

00:37:18.533 --> 00:37:19.833
I change the names.

00:37:19.833 --> 00:37:23.866
I change the level of the measurement
or the type of the variable

00:37:23.866 --> 00:37:29.766
for some of them, say, for instance,
from continuous or quantitative to ordinal

00:37:30.166 --> 00:37:33.966
to nominal or categorical,
and then I change labels.

00:37:33.966 --> 00:37:38.500
And so this is a very important
in terms of preparing the data in Zimbabwe

00:37:38.766 --> 00:37:43.933
because it's going to make it much easier
for you to interpret the analysis

00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:47.866
and then in turn to make sense of it,
especially when you're collaborating

00:37:47.866 --> 00:37:50.800
with a colleague
or potentially working for a client.

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:54.500
One of the most common transformations

00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:57.466
on data is average in several variables.

00:37:57.600 --> 00:37:59.833
That way you can get it, for instance,
a scale score.

00:38:00.100 --> 00:38:05.833
It's also a great way of helping balance
out the error variance of different scores

00:38:05.833 --> 00:38:09.066
and really get you more generalizable
information.

00:38:09.733 --> 00:38:11.733
This is easy to do in Zimbabwe.

00:38:12.033 --> 00:38:14.400
What I'm going to do
is I'm going to take this data set.

00:38:14.400 --> 00:38:18.133
It has ID and it has these three
rating scale questions

00:38:18.866 --> 00:38:21.600
and they're all on a 1 to 5 scale
and they ask people how much they liked

00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:24.333
different elements of,
for instance, your website.

00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:29.066
And I'm going to click on each of these
first or go to like website

00:38:29.300 --> 00:38:32.866
and we have a little bit
of descriptive text and it's a continuous

00:38:32.866 --> 00:38:35.533
or quantitative variable
that's just on a 1 to 5.

00:38:36.100 --> 00:38:40.066
If we go to like price,
you see it's ordinal

00:38:40.066 --> 00:38:43.266
and even though it's ordinal,
you get to specify levels.

00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:45.600
Now it just has the 1 to 5. That's to do.

00:38:46.433 --> 00:38:50.366
And then like product
you see here in the data, it has text,

00:38:50.366 --> 00:38:54.666
it says neither strongly disagree
and so on and it's coded as nominal.

00:38:54.666 --> 00:38:56.366
On the other hand, it's important to say

