04:43:07.566 --> 04:43:10.366
And so take your pick one or other.

04:43:10.366 --> 04:43:12.000
I generally do principal component

04:43:12.000 --> 04:43:16.166
because I prefer that
it starts with the individual variables

04:43:16.166 --> 04:43:20.100
and then infers something about a factor
that goes to them as opposed to

04:43:20.100 --> 04:43:23.766
the idea that the factor is first
and it leads to the individual variables,

04:43:24.300 --> 04:43:26.933
but fundamentally they're going
to accomplish the same thing.

04:43:26.933 --> 04:43:28.666
They're going to help you find
which are your variables,

04:43:28.666 --> 04:43:32.866
go with the others and give you the option
of then combining them

04:43:33.066 --> 04:43:37.433
to get more stable, reliable data
and the smaller number

04:43:37.433 --> 04:43:40.033
of variables that you have to deal with
when you're your analysis.

04:43:40.566 --> 04:43:43.866
Either
one of these will help you find the sense

04:43:43.866 --> 04:43:47.700
and the commonalities in your data
and help you improve your analysis.

04:43:48.933 --> 04:43:51.133
One of the most amazing things
about your movie

04:43:51.133 --> 04:43:56.433
is that this free, simple, friendly,
open source analysis package

04:43:56.700 --> 04:43:59.933
includes
some incredibly high end analyzes.

04:44:00.300 --> 04:44:04.766
In fact, the most surprising one for me
is the inclusion of confirmatory factor

04:44:04.766 --> 04:44:09.300
analysis, something that, for instance,
not even possible to do in SPSS.

04:44:09.300 --> 04:44:12.600
You're on a macintosh,
and if you're doing it in other programs,

04:44:12.600 --> 04:44:15.566
it gets really,
really complicated, really fast.

04:44:16.033 --> 04:44:20.300
And this is by far the easiest and fastest

04:44:20.300 --> 04:44:24.100
and cheapest way
to do a very sophisticated procedure.

04:44:24.400 --> 04:44:27.433
What confirmatory factor
analysis or CFA is

04:44:27.766 --> 04:44:32.900
is an attempt to data and say we know how
the data is supposed to combine.

04:44:33.100 --> 04:44:34.433
We know that these ten variables

04:44:34.433 --> 04:44:38.066
should go to this factor,
these ten should go to this other factor.

04:44:38.333 --> 04:44:42.266
It allows you to specify those factors
and see how well your data

04:44:42.266 --> 04:44:44.866
fit your hypothesized factor structure.

04:44:45.266 --> 04:44:47.466
It also allows you, by the way, to compare

04:44:47.900 --> 04:44:50.533
the fit of factor structures
across two different samples.

04:44:50.733 --> 04:44:52.200
That's a different thing.

